course: dictionary
lesson: 12410
title: Dits and dahs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dah is a word with a special job in Morse code. Morse code sends messages with long and short sounds or flashes. The long one is called dah, and the short one is called dit. Dah is written as a dash: −.
explain: «The sender tapped dit-dah for the letter A.» That means one short tap, then one long tap. So A is dit-dah, written as ·−. Read the pattern from left to right, just as you read words.
explain: People also say «dah» when they show something proudly. «Ta-dah!» is what a magician shouts when the rabbit appears from the hat. Here dah is a sound, not a signal. Look at the words around it to tell which meaning is which.
fact: Dah is the long sound or signal in Morse code.
fact: Dit is the short sound or signal in Morse code.
fact: The letter A is dit-dah, written as ·−.
fact: SOS is dit-dit-dit, dah-dah-dah, dit-dit-dit.
fact: «Ta-dah!» is a proud sound people say when they reveal something, like a magic trick.
exercise: In Morse code, what is the long signal called? | dit | ta-dah | *dah | SOS
exercise: «The letter A is dit-dah in Morse code.» Which pattern shows A? | −−− | *·− | −·− | ···
exercise: «Ta-dah!» shouted by a magician means what? | The magician has lost a long signal | *The magician has finished a trick and is showing it off | The magician is sending a message in Morse code | The magician is sad about the rabbit
test: What is the short signal in Morse code called? | *dit | SOS | dah | ta-dah
test: In «dit-dit-dit, dah-dah-dah, dit-dit-dit», what message is sent? | Dash | *SOS | Ta-dah | Hello
exam: Which sentence uses dah as a sound people make, not as a Morse signal? | «The sender tapped dit-dah.» | «Dah is written as a dash.» | «The sender sent a long dah.» | *«Ta-dah! The rabbit is out of the hat.»
